.056,56.8 214.72399999999996,56.400000000000006 216.39999999999992,56.000000000000014 218.08400000000006,55.599999999999994 219.776,55.19999999999999 221.47599999999997,54.80000000000001 223.18399999999994,54.400000000000006 224.90000000000006,53.999999999999986 226.62400000000002,53.599999999999994 228.356,53.2 230.09599999999995,52.80000000000001 231.84400000000008,52.39999999999998 233.60000000000002,52 235.364,51.599999999999994 237.13599999999997,51.20000000000002 238.91600000000008,50.79999999999998 240.70400000000004,50.39999999999998 242.5,50 244.30399999999995,49.60000000000002 246.11599999999993,49.20000000000002 247.93600000000004,48.79999999999998 249.764,48.400000000000006 251.59999999999997,48 253.44399999999993,47.60000000000002 255.29600000000005,47.19999999999999 257.156,46.80000000000001 259.024,46.400000000000006 260.8999999999999,46 262.78400000000005,45.599999999999994 264.67600000000004,45.19999999999999 266.576,44.80000000000001 268.4839999999999,44.400000000000006 270.4000000000001,44 272.324,43.599999999999994 274.256,43.19999999999999 276.1959999999999,42.80000000000001 278.14400000000006,42.39999999999998 280.1,42 282.06399999999996,41.599999999999994 284.03599999999994,41.20000000000002 286.0160000000001,40.79999999999998 288.004,40.39999999999998 290,40 292.00399999999996,39.60000000000002 294.0159999999999,39.20000000000002 296.03600000000006,38.79999999999998 298.06399999999996,38.400000000000006 300.09999999999997,38 302.1439999999999,37.60000000000002 304.196,37.19999999999999 306.25600000000003,36.80000000000001 308.32399999999996,36.400000000000006 310.3999999999999,36 312.48400000000004,35.599999999999994 314.576,35.19999999999999 316.67599999999993,34.80000000000001 318.78399999999993,34.400000000000006 320.9000000000001,34 323.024,33.599999999999994 325.156,33.19999999999999 327.29599999999994,32.80000000000001 329.4440000000001,32.39999999999998 331.6,32 333.764,31.599999999999994 335.9359999999999,31.200000000000017 338.1160000000001,30.799999999999983 340.30400000000003,30.399999999999977 342.5,30 344.70399999999995,29.600000000000023 346.9159999999999,29.200000000000017 349.1360000000001,28.799999999999983 351.36400000000003,28.400000000000006 353.59999999999997,28 355.84399999999994,27.600000000000023 358.09600000000006,27.19999999999999 360.356,26.80000000000001 362.624,26.400000000000006 364.9,26 367.1840000000001,25.599999999999994 369.476,25.19999999999999 371.77599999999995,24.80000000000001 374.08399999999995,24.400000000000006 376.4000000000001,24 378.72400000000005,23.599999999999994 381.0559999999999,23.19999999999999 383.3959999999999,22.80000000000001 385.74400000000014,22.399999999999977 388.1,22 390.464,21.599999999999994 392.8359999999999,21.200000000000017 395.2160000000001,20.799999999999983 397.60400000000004,20.399999999999977 400,20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"red\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"220\" r=\"3\" fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\"></circle><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"180\" r=\"3\" fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\"></circle><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"140\" r=\"3\" fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\"></circle><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"100\" r=\"3\" fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\"></circle><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"60\" r=\"3\" fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\"></circle><polygon points=\"3,0 -3,-3 -3,3\" fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\" transform=\"translate(400,20) rotate(-9.462322208025617)\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"200\" y=\"200\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"90\" y=\"160\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"-6\" y=\"132\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"86\" y=\"100\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"200\" y=\"60\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject></svg><figcaption>The parabola defined parametrically by x = t² − 1, y = t + 1, t ∈ ℝ.</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"Although the curve in this example is more easily identified when the parameter is eliminated, there is a loss of information in going to the nonparametric form. Specifically, we lose the sense of the curve as the path of a moving point and hence also the direction of the curve.\n\n!!! example \"Sketch the parametric curve\"\n\n\t```math\n\tx=t^3-3t\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad y=t^2\\,,\\quad -2\\le t\\le 2\\,.\n\t```\n\n\tWe could eliminate the parameter and obtain\n\n\t```math\n\tx^2=t^2\\left(t^2-3\\right)^2=y\\left(y-3\\right)^2\\,,\n\t```\n\n\tbut this doesn’t help much since we do not recognize this curve from its Cartesian equation. Instead, let us calculate the coordinates of some points.\n\t\n\tNote that the curve is symmetric about the ``y``-axis because ``x`` is an odd function of ``t`` and ``y`` is an even function of ``t``.\n\n\tThe curve intersects itself on the ``y``-axis. To find this selfintersection, set ``x=0``:\n\n\t```math\n\t0=x=t^3-3t=t\\left(t-\\sqrt 3\\right)\\left(t+\\sqrt 3\\right)\\,.\n\t```\n\n\tFor ``t=0`` the curve is at ``\\left(0,0\\right)``, but for ``t=\\pm\\sqrt 3`` the curve is at ``\\left(0,3\\right)``. The selfintersection occurs because the curve passes through the same point for two different values of the parameter.","output":"","result":"Although the curve in this example is more easily identified when the parameter is eliminated, there is a loss of information in going to the nonparametric form. Specifically, we lose the sense of the curve as the path of a moving point and hence also the direction of the curve.\n\n!!! example \"Sketch the parametric curve\"\n\n\t```math\n\tx=t^3-3t\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad y=t^2\\,,\\quad -2\\le t\\le 2\\,.\n\t```\n\n\tWe could eliminate the parameter and obtain\n\n\t```math\n\tx^2=t^2\\left(t^2-3\\right)^2=y\\left(y-3\\right)^2\\,,\n\t```\n\n\tbut this doesn’t help much since we do not recognize this curve from its Cartesian equation. Instead, let us calculate the coordinates of some points.\n\t\n\tNote that the curve is symmetric about the ``y``-axis because ``x`` is an odd function of ``t`` and ``y`` is an even function of ``t``.\n\n\tThe curve intersects itself on the ``y``-axis. To find this selfintersection, set ``x=0``:\n\n\t```math\n\t0=x=t^3-3t=t\\left(t-\\sqrt 3\\right)\\left(t+\\sqrt 3\\right)\\,.\n\t```\n\n\tFor ``t=0`` the curve is at ``\\left(0,0\\right)``, but for ``t=\\pm\\sqrt 3`` the curve is at ``\\left(0,3\\right)``. The selfintersection occurs because the curve passes through the same point for two different values of the parameter.","resultHTML":"<p>Although the curve in this example is more easily identified when the parameter is eliminated, there is a loss of information in going to the nonparametric form. Specifically, we lose the sense of the curve as the path of a moving point and hence also the direction of the curve.</p>\n<aside data-type=\"example\">\n<h5>Sketch the parametric curve</h5>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\nx=t^3-3t\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad y=t^2\\,,\\quad -2\\le t\\le 2\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>We could eliminate the parameter and obtain</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\nx^2=t^2\\left(t^2-3\\right)^2=y\\left(y-3\\right)^2\\,,\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>but this doesn’t help much since we do not recognize this curve from its Cartesian equation. Instead, let us calculate the coordinates of some points.</p>\n<p>Note that the curve is symmetric about the <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(y\\)</span>-axis because <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(x\\)</span> is an odd function of <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(t\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(y\\)</span> is an even function of <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(t\\)</span>.</p>\n<p>The curve intersects itself on the <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(y\\)</span>-axis. To find this selfintersection, set <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(x=0\\)</span>:</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n0=x=t^3-3t=t\\left(t-\\sqrt 3\\right)\\left(t+\\sqrt 3\\right)\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>For <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(t=0\\)</span> the curve is at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left(0,0\\right)\\)</span>, but for <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(t=\\pm\\sqrt 3\\)</span> the curve is at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left(0,3\\right)\\)</span>. The selfintersection occurs because the curve passes through the same point for two different values of the parameter.</p>\n</aside>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 50;\nconst xmid = 3 * scale;\nconst ymid = 4.5 * scale;\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n  width: 6.5 * scale,\n  height: 5 * scale,\n  caption: \"A self-intersecting parametric curve.\",\n});\n\nfigure.axes({ origin: [xmid, ymid], scale });\nfigure.label(\"O\", {\n  x: xmid - 16, y: ymid, width: 14, height: 28, latex: true,\n});\n\nfigure.curve((t) => [t ** 3 - 3 * t, t ** 2], {\n  domain: [-2, 2],\n  samples: 401,\n  stroke: \"red\",\n  width: 1,\n});\n\nfor (const t of [-2, -1, 0, 1, Math.sqrt(3)]) {\n  figure.point(t ** 3 - 3 * t, t ** 2, {\n    radius: 3, fill: \"red\", stroke: \"red\",\n  });\n}\n\n// Arrow at t = 2, pointing in the direction of increasing t.\nfigure.polygon()\n  .points(\"3,0 -3,-3 -3,3\")\n  .fill(\"red\")\n  .stroke(\"red\")\n  .transform(\n    `translate(${xmid + 2 * scale},${ymid - 4 * scale}) ` +\n    `rotate(${Math.atan2(-4, 9) * 180 / Math.PI})`\n  );\n\nfor (const [label, dx, dy] of [\n  [\"t=-2\", -3, -4.15],\n  [\"t=-1\", 2.15, -1.15],\n  [\"t=0\", 0.05, 0.05],\n  [\"t=1\", -2.85, -1.15],\n  [String.raw`t=\\pm\\sqrt 3`, 0.1, -3.15],\n]) {\n  figure.label(label, {\n    x: xmid + dx * scale,\n    y: ymid + dy * scale,\n    width: 70,\n    height: 28,\n    latex: true,\n  });\n}\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xyOt=−2t=−1t=0t=1t=±3A self-intersecting parametric curve.","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"325\" height=\"250\" viewBox=\"0 0 325 250\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"225\" x2=\"325\" y2=\"225\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"325,225 318,221 318,229\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"150,0 146,7 154,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"311\" y=\"195\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"158\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"134\" y=\"225\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>O</mi></math></div></foreignObject><polyline points=\"50,25 54.470049999999986,26.995000000000005 58.88040000000001,28.980000000000018 63.23134999999999,30.955000000000013 67.52320000000003,32.920000000000016 71.75625000000001,34.875 75.93080000000003,36.82000000000002 80.04715000000004,38.754999999999995 84.10560000000001,40.68000000000001 88.10645,42.595 92.05000000000001,44.5 95.93655000000001,46.39500000000001 99.76640000000003,48.28 103.53984999999994,50.15499999999997 107.25720000000005,52.02000000000001 110.91875,53.87499999999997 114.5248,55.72 11