.16760268682388,123.23546014664348 125.02027510507213,123.07384237283372 124.87317286155195,122.9172500849468 124.72641661273207,122.76564346814168 124.58012585188236,122.61898010403056 124.4344188553029,122.47721499787916 124.28941262914158,122.34030060689567 124.14522285682226,122.20818686959582 124.00196384710482,122.08082123623144 123.85974848279865,121.95814870026906 123.71868817015024,121.84011183090523 123.57889278892624,121.72665080660444 123.44047064321165,121.61770344964506 123.30352841294417,121.51320526165868 123.16817110620383,121.41308946014732 123.03450201227793,121.31728701596315 122.90262265552036,121.22572669173448 122.7726327500242,121.13833508122164 122.64463015512614,121.05503664958601 122.51871083176106,120.97575377455497 122.3949687996846,120.90040678846528 122.27349609558117,120.82891402116692 122.15438273207458,120.76119184376945 122.03771665765824,120.69715471321179 121.92358371756103,120.636715217637 121.81206761556514,120.5797841225527 121.70324987679139,120.5262704177573 121.59720981146722,120.47608136501276 121.49402447969233,120.429122546443 121.39376865721616,120.38529791363818 121.29651480224145,120.34450983744362 121.2023330232674,120.3066591584127 121.1112910479854,120.27164523790208 121.02345419324035,120.23936600978814 120.93888533606962,120.20971803278253 120.85764488583165,120.18259654332479 120.77979075743549,120.15789550903004 120.70537834568236,120.13550768266892 120.63446050072952,120.11532465665731 120.56708750468665,120.0972369180328 120.50330704935435,120.0811339038949 120.4431642151136,120.06690405728541 120.38670145097517,120.05443488348601 120.33395855579685,120.0436130067088 120.28497266067636,120.03432422715649 120.23977821252699,120.02645357842798 120.19840695884278,120.01988538524535 120.16088793365961,120.01450332147814 120.12724744471748,120.01019046844034 120.09750906182983,120.00682937343582 120.07169360646417,120.00430210852763 120.04981914253854,120.00249032950639 120.0319009684375,120.00127533503336 120.01795161025082,120.00053812593295 120.00798081623783,120.00015946461019 120.00199555251947,120.00001993456809 120,120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"red\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline></svg><figcaption>A cardioid.</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"## Slopes, Areas, and Arc Lengths for Polar Curves\n\n::: proposition\nAt any point ``P`` other than the origin on the polar curve ``r=f\\left(\\theta\\right)``, the angle ``\\psi`` between the radial line from the origin to ``P`` and the tangent to the curve is given by\n\n```math\n\\tan\\psi=\\frac{f\\left(\\theta\\right)}{f^\\prime\\left(\\theta\\right)}\\,.\n```\n\nIn particular, ``\\psi=\\frac{\\uppi}{2}`` if ``f^\\prime\\left(\\theta\\right)=0``. If ``f\\left(\\theta_0\\right)=0`` and the curve has a tangent line at ``\\theta_0``, then that tangent line has equation ``\\theta=\\theta_0``.\n:::\n\n\n","output":"","result":"## Slopes, Areas, and Arc Lengths for Polar Curves\n\n::: proposition\nAt any point ``P`` other than the origin on the polar curve ``r=f\\left(\\theta\\right)``, the angle ``\\psi`` between the radial line from the origin to ``P`` and the tangent to the curve is given by\n\n```math\n\\tan\\psi=\\frac{f\\left(\\theta\\right)}{f^\\prime\\left(\\theta\\right)}\\,.\n```\n\nIn particular, ``\\psi=\\frac{\\uppi}{2}`` if ``f^\\prime\\left(\\theta\\right)=0``. If ``f\\left(\\theta_0\\right)=0`` and the curve has a tangent line at ``\\theta_0``, then that tangent line has equation ``\\theta=\\theta_0``.\n:::\n\n\n","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-ES111_071Lecture07-c3910-slopes-areas-and-arc-lengths-for-polar-curves\">\n<h1>Slopes, Areas, and Arc Lengths for Polar Curves</h1>\n<div data-type=\"proposition\">\n<p>At any point <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(P\\)</span> other than the origin on the polar curve <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(r=f\\left(\\theta\\right)\\)</span>, the angle <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\psi\\)</span> between the radial line from the origin to <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(P\\)</span> and the tangent to the curve is given by</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\tan\\psi=\\frac{f\\left(\\theta\\right)}{f^\\prime\\left(\\theta\\right)}\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>In particular, <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\psi=\\frac{\\uppi}{2}\\)</span> if <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f^\\prime\\left(\\theta\\right)=0\\)</span>. If <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\left(\\theta_0\\right)=0\\)</span> and the curve has a tangent line at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\theta_0\\)</span>, then that tangent line has equation <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\theta=\\theta_0\\)</span>.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 60;\nconst xmid = scale;\nconst ymid = 2 * scale;\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n  width: 2.5 * scale,\n  height: 3 * scale,\n  caption: \"The area between two polar curves.\",\n});\n\nfigure.axes({ origin: [xmid, ymid], scale });\nfigure.label(\"O\", {\n  x: xmid - 16, y: ymid, width: 14, height: 28, latex: true,\n});\n\nconst r1 = (theta) => Math.SQRT2 * Math.sin(theta);\nconst r2 = (theta) => Math.sqrt(Math.sin(2 * theta));\nconst polar = (r, theta) => [r(theta) * Math.cos(theta), r(theta) * Math.sin(theta)];\n\nconst area = [];\nfor (const [r, start, end] of [\n  [r1, 0, Math.PI / 4],\n  [r2, Math.PI / 4, Math.PI / 2],\n]) {\n  for (let i = 0; i <= 79; i++) {\n    const theta = start + (end - start) * i / 79;\n    const [x, y] = polar(r, theta);\n    area.push(`${xmid + scale * x},${ymid - scale * y}`);\n  }\n}\nfigure.polygon().points(area.join(\" \")).fill(\"lightblue\").stroke(\"none\");\n\nfigure.curve((theta) => polar(r1, theta), {\n  domain: [0, Math.PI], samples: 315, stroke: \"red\", width: 1,\n});\nfigure.curve((theta) => polar(r2, theta), {\n  domain: [0, Math.PI / 2], samples: 158, stroke: \"green\", width: 1,\n});\nfigure.curve((theta) => polar(r2, theta), {\n  domain: [Math.PI + 0.01, 3 * Math.PI / 2],\n  samples: 157, stroke: \"green\", width: 1,\n});\n\nfigure.plot((x) => x, {\n  domain: [0, 1], samples: 101, stroke: \"black\", width: 1, dash: \"1\",\n});\nfigure.label(String.raw`\\frac{\\pi}{4}`, {\n  x: xmid + scale,\n  y: ymid - 1.25 * scale,\n  width: 28,\n  height: 36,\n  latex: true,\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xyOπ4The area between two polar curves.","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"150\" height=\"180\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 180\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"150,120 143,116 143,124\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"60,0 56,7 64,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"136\" y=\"90\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"68\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"44\" y=\"120\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>O</mi></math></div></foreignObject><polygon points=\"60,120 60.84352978336768,119.99161356239848 61.686726085282885,119.96645756509201 62.52925555613187,119.92454195326415 63.37078510992616,119.86588329785215 64.21098205598497,119.7905047889958 65.04951423046128,119.69843622686948 65.8860501276596,119.58971400990086 66.72025903109363,119.46438112038119 67.55181114423189,119.32248710747268 68.38037772087954,119.16408806761962 69.20563119514513,118.98924662237128 70.02724531094066,118.79803189362502 70.84489525096373,118.59051947629965 71.65825776511107,118.36679140844964 72.46701129827227,118.12693613883225